<h2>Where Residential Claims Often Fall Short</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Partial roof scopes</strong> that repair a few slopes when damage is spread across the roof, or that leave out items such as drip edge, underlayment, and code-required components.</li>
<li><strong>Interior damage left out</strong> because the adjuster did not inspect closets, attics, or behind furniture.</li>
<li><strong>Low unit pricing</strong> that does not reflect local labor and material costs after a large storm.</li>
<li><strong>Depreciation</strong> applied heavily to items with years of useful life left.</li>
<li><strong>Additional living expense</strong> not requested or not fully documented.</li>
<li><strong>Code upgrades</strong> left off the estimate. Corpus Christi requires a permit to re-roof, and the city's submission includes a TDI WPI-1 form from the windstorm engineer or inspector. Ordinance or law coverage, if your policy includes it, may help with code-related costs up to its limit. Our <a href="/local-building-codes/">local building codes</a> page has details.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What to Do After Damage to Your Home</h2>
<ol>
<li>Make sure everyone is safe, and stay away from downed lines and standing water.</li>
<li>Photograph and video the damage before cleanup, inside and out.</li>
<li>Make reasonable temporary repairs to prevent further damage and keep receipts.</li>
<li>Report the loss to every insurer that may be involved, and write down claim numbers.</li>
<li>Keep a log of every call, email, and inspection.</li>
<li>Do not throw away damaged materials until they have been documented.</li>
</ol>
<p>Our <a href="/claim-documentation-checklist/">claim documentation checklist</a> can help you stay organized.</p>

<h2>How a Corpus Christi Public Adjuster Can Help Homeowners</h2>
<p>We inspect the home, review each policy, prepare a line-item estimate in Xactimate, and gather photos, measurements, and supporting records. We then present the claim and handle communication with the insurer, including reinspections and supplements. If the claim stalls or a payment seems low, we can help you understand options such as <a href="/services/insurance-claim-supplements/">supplements</a> or the policy's appraisal clause. We cannot guarantee a result; outcomes depend on your policy and the facts.</p>
<p>Fees are disclosed in a written contract before any work begins; Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement. To talk through your home claim, request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a>.</p>
